<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5f929f3e9bc2a4e1733907745e24e47aa92d1156" commit="5715ab75df98b7ef91104d025c6cf637a9e7f7ee" commit_message="glibc: backport an patch to fix [BZ 19329]  This backports a pending CL from https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=19329 to fix the issue.  The commit message is This fixes a subset of the issues described in https://sourceware.org/ml/libc-alpha/2016-11/msg01026.html without adding locks to pthread_create.  Only races between dlopen and pthread_create were considered, and the asserts got removed that tried to check for concurrency issues.  The patch is incomplete because dlclose, tls access and dl_iterate_phdr related code paths are not modified.  dlclose should be updated in a similar fashion to dlopen to make the patch complete alternatively pthread_create may take the GL(dl_load_write_lock) to sync with dlclose or the GL(dl_load_lock) to sync with dlopen and dlclose (that would simplify the concurrency design, but increase lock contention on the locks).  2016-11-30  Szabolcs Nagy  &lt;szabolcs.nagy@arm.com&gt;   [BZ #19329]  * elf/dl-open.c (dl_open_worker): Write GL(dl_tls_generation)  atomically.  * elf/dl-tls.c (_dl_allocate_tls_init): Read GL(dl_tls_generation),  GL(dl_tls_max_dtv_idx), slotinfo entries and listp-&gt;next atomically.  Remove assertions that cannot be guaranteed.  (_dl_add_to_slotinfo): Write the slotinfo entries and listp-&gt;next  atomically.  BUG=chromium:783832 TEST=cbuildbot chromiuos-sdk falco-llvm-toolchain      kevin-llvm-toolchain caroline-llvm-toolchain      daisy-llvm-toolchain  Change-Id: I5f929f3e9bc2a4e1733907745e24e47aa92d1156 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/883568 Commit-Ready: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: George Burgess &lt;gbiv@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="883568" owner_email="yunlian@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/68/883568/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0c2fdad02af0ede3f744d6e14543b47072329b72" commit="846876430c83d7ecff1d95683982e94dfd60f643" commit_message="Increase palm zone width for eve  Palms around the edge of the touchpad should be ignored. This CL tunes the palm edge zone width to allow fingers to be detected along the edge, but reject palm touches while typing  BUG=b:70891705 TEST=Manually tested on eve, added touchtest test.  Change-Id: I0c2fdad02af0ede3f744d6e14543b47072329b72 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/881948 Commit-Ready: Sean O'Brien &lt;seobrien@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sean O'Brien &lt;seobrien@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tai-hsu Lin &lt;sheckylin@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="881948" owner_email="seobrien@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/xorg-conf" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/xorg-conf" ref="refs/changes/48/881948/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5d225f00ad73ae865fb220841d9521c8166d5508" commit="6d86a10bee4c528118ac84188dbc57729d75e49a" commit_message="Add test for touches while typing on eve  Palms around the edge of the touchpad should be ignored. This CL adds a test where the user is typing and getting unwanted cursor movement.  BUG=b:70891705 TEST=None  Change-Id: I5d225f00ad73ae865fb220841d9521c8166d5508 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/881947 Commit-Ready: Sean O'Brien &lt;seobrien@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Sean O'Brien &lt;seobrien@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tai-hsu Lin &lt;sheckylin@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="881947" owner_email="seobrien@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/touchpad-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touchpad-tests" ref="refs/changes/47/881947/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ief0e999ed52f39420eed5f07432273e741a14c7e" commit="68a920725907e627eae3ee89b3a7bf777f9c0e7a" commit_message="usb pd: Increasing delay for Rp time on CC lines  Some chargers don't respect the SRC.Open state within the 20ms allotted by the usb spec. The LiteOn Charger seems to notice after ~120ms bumping to 200ms so we cutoff Vbus for even ill-behaved chargers. We expect to brown out in the sleep.  BRANCH=none TEST=LiteOn charge will disconnect now BUG=b:72510370  Change-Id: Ief0e999ed52f39420eed5f07432273e741a14c7e Signed-off-by: Jett Rink &lt;jettrink@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/886833 Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="886833" owner_email="jettrink@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/33/886833/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I0197da5ca3f880993b7c228c9ef1fd6bde1e68c9" commit="ce07dbfa29db084031b089cac57faa37fdaefb80" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: enable FBC on Stoney  Enable CONFIG_DRM_AMD_DC_FBC which is a power saving feature on stoney. Used the below command to enable:  echo &quot;CONFIG_DRM_AMD_DC_FBC=y&quot; &gt;&gt; chromeos/config/x86_64/chromeos-amd-stoneyridge.flavour.config chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig  BUG=b:72411207 TEST=boot on kahle, verified FBC is enabled      run graphics_SanAngeles  Change-Id: I0197da5ca3f880993b7c228c9ef1fd6bde1e68c9 Signed-off-by: Shirish S &lt;shirish.s@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/867798 Reviewed-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; " 